{"availability":"available","full":"compcode-solutions/contoso-policy-assistant","name":"contoso-policy-assistant","description":"Permission-aware RAG policy assistant: role-based access applied before vector search, supervisor-approved ticket creation, 14 golden evals. .NET 8 + React. Live demo","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"C#","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-19T16:54:18Z","updated":"2026-10-06T06:29:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://policy.compcodesolutions.com","topics":["access-control","dotnet","evals","gemini","guardrails","human-in-the-loop","llm","rag","rbac","react","retrieval-augmented-generation","typescript"],"demo":"https://policy.compcodesolutions.com/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:22.899Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:22.899Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:22.899Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T22:39:22.899Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Built and maintained by CompCode Solutions (Bengaluru): AI systems that reach production. Live demo · Write-up · Work with us","Most RAG implementations retrieve first and filter by permission afterwards. That leaks — and this repository shows the alternative, with the code and a test.","Filtering after retrieval leaks in two ways. The obvious one is metadata: restricted chunks were retrieved, so they leave fingerprints in citation counts, traces, token logs and debug endpoints. The subtle one is top-K starvation — if the ten nearest chunks are all restricted, an uncleared user gets \"I don't know\" while a cleared user gets a confident cited answer. That difference is itself information about what the corpus contains."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/compcode-solutions/contoso-policy-assistant/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"7dbf0463cdeb5862ec5d680edd1969b7780d2d4ff442c28c1190b8ca8ccd044c","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T22:39:23.066